@startuml

title Restoring the feeds

hide footbox
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left

participant "Provisioning" as prov
participant "Synthetic service" as syn
database "Feed configs" as db
participant "IAM" as iam
participant "Marketdata" as md

== The service starts ==

syn -> db : list the active tenants
loop each tenant, the system tenant first
    syn -> db : read the collections and feeds\nin the tenant, through its root party
    loop each feed with enabled and auto_start
        alt the collection holds a run grant
            syn -> iam : iam.v1.ops.exchange_run_grant(grant id, run id)\nAuthorization: the service's own token
            iam --> syn : run token, or refused (grant lapsed)
        end
        alt a token is held, or the feed has a fixed price
            syn -> md : read the vintage series and observations\nAuthorization: the run token
            syn -> syn : start the feed
        else the feed has no token, or a dependency did not answer
            syn -> syn : keep the feed in the retry set and log the reason
        end
    end
end

== A dependency was not ready ==

loop the retry set is not empty, 2 s doubling to 30 s, at most five minutes
    syn -> syn : wait
    syn -> syn : start each feed of the retry set as above
end
syn -> syn : log an error for each feed that still fails

== A provision creates feeds ==

prov -> syn : synthetic.v1.ops.restore_feeds\nAuthorization: the provisioning administrator
syn -> syn : one pass for the caller's tenant, no retry
syn --> prov : the feeds started and the reason for each failure

note over syn
    A restore uses the same exchange as the Start command.
    No person is present, so the stored consent stands in for the operator.
    A restore creates no binding: the stored bindings stand.
end note

@enduml
